{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CurvatureRankGbStratification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CurvatureRankGbStratification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Operations","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.SuccPred.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ENat.Lattice"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_formula_stratification_existence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_formula_stratification_existence","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L136-L158","doc":"**Mass-formula stratification (statement form).**\nThe Markov-trace pairing `tr : A → R` decomposes as a\ntelescoping sum over GB strata:\n\n  tr T = Σ_{r=0}^∞ [tr (T mod J^{r+1}) - tr (T mod J^r)]\n\nEach term is the trace of the curvature-rank-`r` stratum\ncontribution.  This is the categorical statement; the explicit\nsix-term identification is in\n`prop:curvature-rank-gb-stratification` (.md).  ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.gbDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.gbDepth","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L128-L134","doc":"**Curvature-rank is the GB filtration depth** (corollary of the\nstructure proved above): the unique non-negative integer `r`\nsuch that `T ∈ J^r \\ J^{r+1}`, when finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_strict_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_strict_chain","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L118-L124","doc":"**Theorem (chain-strict at non-zero strata).** If the stratum\n`r` is non-empty (i.e. there is some `T` with `InStratum Φ r T`),\nthen `J (r+1) ⊊ J r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.inStratum_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.inStratum_unique","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L98-L116","doc":"**Theorem (strata are disjoint).** An element cannot have two\ndistinct curvature-ranks.  Equivalently: the strata of a\nfiltered algebra are mutually exclusive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.InStratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.InStratum","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L92-L96","doc":"An element of curvature-rank exactly `r` lives in `J r` but\nnot in `J (r+1)` (the strict-stratum characterisation).\nThis is the `r`-th associated-graded layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank_mul_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank_mul_ge","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L81-L90","doc":"**Sub-additivity of curvature-rank** under the algebra\nmultiplication.  This is the structural manifestation of\n`J m * J n ⊆ J (m+n)`: the rank of a product `T₁ * T₂` is at\nleast the sum of the individual ranks (whenever both are finite). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L74-L79","doc":"The curvature-rank of any element is at least 0 (since\nevery element belongs to `J 0 = ⊤`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.curvatureRank","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The CURVATURE-RANK of `T` is the largest `n` such that `T ∈ J n`,\nextended to `ℕ∞` (∞ when T = 0, since 0 lives in every ideal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mem_J_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mem_J_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L59-L67","doc":"Membership in `J k` is decreasing in `k`: if `T ∈ J k` and\n`m ≤ k` then `T ∈ J m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mem_J_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mem_J_zero","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L54-L57","doc":"Every element belongs to `J 0` (which is the whole algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_mul","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_decreasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_decreasing","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_zero_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J_zero_top","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.J","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FilteredAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/curvature-rank-gb-stratification.lean#L40-L47","doc":"A filtered algebra: a `R`-algebra `A` with a decreasing\nmultiplicative filtration `J : ℕ → Ideal A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}